  "query_preview": "..\n\nHigh pressure brings pleasant weather to SE Mi during the early week \nperiod. It ensures dry conditions and seasonable temperatures with \nlower humidity today and Tuesday. For today, the surface ridge axis \nis positioned to our west which maintains a light but steady \nnortherly low level wind field. Low level dry air advection drops \nsurface Td comfortably down into the mid 50s across the region. Full \nsun and maximum daytime surface heating build a deep boundary layer \nin model soundings that is way too dry for any cumulus during the \nafternoon. Guidance highs in the lower 80s are right at normal values\nfor early August. Onshore flow into the Thumb shoreline keeps \nreadings a few degrees cooler. \n\nHigh pressure slides steadily across Lower Mi tonight and early \nTuesday becoming centered over PA/NY by afternoon. This results in \nlight SW wind into Lower Mi which combines with the mid/upper level \nridge overhead to lift temperatures a few more degrees both Tuesday \nand Wednesday. Guidance highs in the mid 80s look reasonable each \nday while there is a greater mid/high cloud component and an uptick \nin humidity by Wednesday afternoon. \n\nWednesday's cloud and humidity increases are driven by continued SW \nflow between Atlantic coast high pressure and the next low pressure \nand frontal system moving in from the Plains/Midwest. There are \nstill some timing differences among the 00Z deterministic models \nregarding the position of the surface low/front Wednesday and \nWednesday night. Considering the mid/upper level trough spends much \nof the day digging southward into the Plains states, prefer model \nsolutions offering slower eastward frontal progress until Wednesday \nnight and Thursday for SE Mi. It then looks like a slow frontal \npassage through the area Thursday into Friday as the mid/upper level \nlong wave trough hangs to our west while guiding a new short wave \nsystem from the Plains into the Great Lakes. If this feature does \nmaterialize, then it would help nudge the front through Lower Mi into\nOntario/Ohio where it dissipates to begin the weekend.",
